# dbt naming conventions

Use these names when creating or renaming dbt models and their model YAML
files.

## Intermediate and mart models

Use one of:

`<layer>_<domain>__<entity>_(<descriptor>)_(<fiat>)_(<time_grain>)`

For intermediate models intentionally materialized to improve query
performance or to reuse expensive transformations, `int` is also a valid
layer:

`int_<domain>__<entity>_(<descriptor>)_(<fiat>)_(<time_grain>)`

Use `int` only for that performance/reuse purpose, not merely because a model
lives in the intermediate directory.

- `layer`: `fct`, `agg`, `dim`, or qualifying `int`
- `domain`: `blc` (balances and holdings), `trx` (transactions), `prj`
  (projections), `inv` (investing), `mtr` (metrics), `alc` (allocation),
  `sim` (simulations), or `com` (common/shared utilities)
- `entity`: for example `balances`, `holdings`, `rates`, `transactions`, or
  `categories`
- `descriptor`: optional text that makes the model's purpose clear
- `fiat`: include when values are in fiat currency
- `time_grain`: `daily`, `weekly`, `monthly`, `quarterly`, `yearly`, or `eop`
  for multiple grains

## Staging models

Use:

`stg_<domain>__<source>_<descriptor>`

The `source` is the literal source name.

## Model YAML files

Name model YAML files:

`_<layer>_<domain>__models.yml`

When renaming a model, update its SQL filename, `ref()` calls, YAML model
name, and documentation references consistently.
